hexad (gpuwm-hex: the differentiable-engine runner, ad-binder and libhexad_phys)
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see the distribution's LICENSE).

The derivative rules in this crate are the tangent-linear and adjoint forms of the
gpuwm-hex forecast kernels. Where those kernels are ports of MPAS-Atmosphere v8.4.2
(LANL/UCAR) or of the MMM / RRFS physics it calls, the BSD-3-Clause terms and
notices reproduced in the distribution's NOTICE govern the derived portions here
too, and the marking that licence requires applies: this is a modified work, not
the version available from LANS and UCAR.

At run time the runner opens, by path and pinned sha256 taken from the recorded
plan, the CUB / Thrust and cuBLAS host libraries the recorded forecast used (CuPy's
and NVIDIA's). It does not ship or link them.

The Rust crates the two products link are listed with their licence texts in
licenses/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES-helper-binaries.txt (program row D).
